 presidential pardon.\""],[21.39,"Kennedy never actually used the word."],[23.39,"It got little attention at the time."],[25.72,"Three days later, the President was assassinated in Dallas."],[29.22,"The family's planned Thanksgiving at Hyannis Port never happened."],[32.86,"Scoreboard: Turkeys spared, two."],[34.91,"Sort of."],[36.12,"One asterisk each."],[38.24,"Twelve. Nixon And Reagan. The Petting Zoo Era."],[40.85,"Through the 1970s, the presentation became routine."],[44.31,"In 1971, First Lady Pat Nixon presented the turkeys."],[48.49,"Nixon reportedly sent one bird to a petting zoo."],[51.81,"Unofficially."],[52.68,"Ronald Reagan spent Thanksgiving 1985 at his ranch."],[56.79,"A pilot flew over it with a 120-foot banner: \"Happy Thanksgiving Ron and Nancy.\""],[60.86,"Then, 1987."],[63.26,"A reporter asked Reagan whether he would pardon officials in the Iran-Contra affair."],[68.17,"Reagan deflected with a joke about the turkey: \"If they'd given me a different answer on Charlie and his future, I would have pardoned him.\""],[74.8,"Charlie was already headed to a petting zoo."],[77.26,"The word \"pardon\" was now attached to a turkey."],[79.96,"As a joke."],[80.82,"Two years later, it stopped being a joke."],[83.22,"Thirteen. George H.W. Bush. It'S Official."],[85.42,"November 17th, 1989."],[88.3,"Two hundred years after Washington's first proclamation."],[91.3,"George H.W."],[91.94,"Bush stands in front of a turkey and says it \"will not end up on anyone's dinner table.\""],[97.35,"Then: \"He's granted a presidential pardon as of right now.\""],[100.25,"And he sent the turkey to live out its days on a children's farm."],[103.03,"That's the moment the official, every-year pardon begins."],[107.38,"Scoreboard: Turkeys spared, with no asterisk: one."],[110.83,"Finally."]],"words":[["eleven",0,0.04],["john",0,0.61],["f",0,0.78],["kennedy",0,0.97],["let",0,1.46],["this",0,1.69],["one",0,1.86],["grow",0,2.01],["november",1,2.38],["19th",1,2.92],["1963",1,3.6],["ke